		<div data-tab-content="help" >
			<p>Custom rules let you examine incoming site traffic and apply an action to the requests that match the criteria you define. Rules are evaluated in the order they are listed. You can drag rules to reorder them when no search filters are applied.</p>
			<p>Cloudflare deprecated Firewall Rules and moved existing firewall rules to custom rules. Rules that used the Allow or Bypass actions now use the Skip action. Your API token needs the <strong>Zone WAF</strong> permission to view and edit custom rules.</p>
			<ul>
				<li><p><strong>Managed Challenge</strong> - Cloudflare dynamically picks the type of challenge that is shown to the visitor, based on the characteristics of the request.</p></li>
				<li><p><strong>Block</strong> - Matching requests are denied access to the site. Pro plans and above can customize the response that is returned.</p></li>
				<li><p><strong>JS Challenge</strong> - The visitor must pass a Cloudflare JavaScript challenge before proceeding.</p></li>
				<li><p><strong>Skip</strong> - Matching requests skip the security features you select, such as the remaining custom rules, rate limiting rules, managed rules, or Super Bot Fight Mode rules.</p></li>
				<li><p><strong>Interactive Challenge</strong> - The visitor must interact with the challenge page before proceeding.</p></li>
				<li><p><strong>Log</strong> - Records matching requests in Cloudflare Logs. Only available on Enterprise plans.</p></li>
			</ul>
